  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/calypsonet/keyple-demo-ticketing/tarball/26.10.22",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/calypsonet/keyple-demo-ticketing/zipball/26.10.22",
  "body": "### Breaking changes\r\n- Components renamed with the English ticketing terms, the applications being installed as new applications (the previous ones are to be uninstalled, and their settings are not taken over):\r\n  - \"inspection\" instead of \"control\": `src/inspection`, `kdt-inspection-app`, application \"Keyple Demo — Inspection\";\r\n  - \"sales\" instead of \"reloading\" for the demo selling and loading the tickets: `src/sales`, `kdt-sales-*` artifacts, applications \"Keyple Demo — Sales\", \"Keyple Demo — Sales (Interop)\", and \"Keyple Demo — Sales (.NET)\".\r\n- Build requirements: Java 17 for all the Java and Kotlin components, .NET 10 for the .NET client, and Node.js 24 for\r\n  the dashboard.\r\n### Added\r\n- Functional documentation (`docs/functional-documentation`): use cases, business rules, and messages of the demo, with diagrams and a glossary, and annexes specifying the data model of the card and the card procedures, in the graphic charter of the CNA documents, attached as PDF and HTML files to each release.\r\n- Unit tests of the business rules (common library, sales server, validation and inspection apps), and CI checks of the log and exception messages, of the architecture of the Android applications, and of the dashboard code.\r\n- Storage cards: anti-passback check in the validation app; on the Famoco terminals, storage cards handled by the validation app, and MIFARE Ultralight cards read by the validation and inspection apps.\r\n- Sales clients: the result screens return automatically after 5 seconds, the remaining time being displayed.\r\n### Changed\r\n- All the applications: same English ticketing vocabulary in the displayed texts (\"ticket\", \"card\", \"Season pass\", \"Multi-trip ticket\", \"Card rejected\", etc.) and English typography; technical messages are no longer displayed (the cause being logged), and the clients display the same messages for the statuses of the server.\r\n- Reactivity of the terminals: the operations on the readers and the sounds run on dedicated threads, the stop of the card detection (about 440 ms on the Bluebird terminals) no longer delaying the display; the inspection result is displayed in an overlay of the card reader screen; the \"Please wait\" indicator is removed.\r\n- Sales clients: same settings screens in both clients (entries checked as they are typed, test of the server, return after saving), and a back arrow on all the screens but the home screen.\r\n- Android applications: version of the release displayed (YY.MM.DD) instead of a fixed \"1.0\".\r\n- Code quality: layered architecture with ports and adapters in the Android applications (Hilt instead of Dagger), sales server split by business operation, remote services and data named after the business operations, same log template in all the components, and conventions described in the README.\r\n- READMEs reviewed against the code and limited to the technical details of the components, the specifications being in the functional documentation; the changelogs of the archived repositories are moved to `docs/history/`.\r\n### Fixed\r\n- Common library: a field value whose high bit is set was truncated when encoded (for example, a counter of 16,777,215 written as 65,535 on a storage card).\r\n- Validation app:\r\n  - anti-passback: a card could be validated again a few seconds after a first validation, debiting a trip twice;\r\n  - Calypso cards: the expired or exhausted contracts are marked in the event when the card is rejected, contracts of unknown type are no longer accepted without debit, and the type of the contract used is its tariff;\r\n  - a card that cannot be selected is rejected, instead of being validated with the data of the previous card;\r\n  - crash at startup with the mocked storage card library, and on an unexpected error of the validation procedure.\r\n- Inspection app: a Calypso contract of an unexpected version rejects the card; the validation period could end 59 seconds too early; the failure sound was given twice.\r\n- Validation and inspection apps: the Bluebird reader can be selected again on Android 13 and later.\r\n- Sales server:\r\n  - loading: the expired contracts keep their priority and their record is reused, a season pass is renewed for 30 days from its end date, a single contract card keeps a usable ticket of another type, and a card without space is rejected instead of a success without writing;\r\n  - a card whose last event has an unexpected version is rejected instead of being loaded;\r\n  - each card gets a unique application number at personalization (it was 1 for all the cards);\r\n  - the server starts without PC/SC reader or SAM;\r\n  - dashboard: transactions no longer lost, missed, or displayed twice.\r\n- Sales Android client: the statuses returned by the server were interpreted with a shift of one (wrong message, screen stuck on the loading animation).\r\n- Sales multiplatform client: an error of the server when reading the card is displayed, instead of an empty card.\r\n- Sales .NET client: the number of trips was sent in hexadecimal (10 trips were refused and 20 trips loaded 14), and the trips could be loaded in another card than the one read.\r\n### Upgraded\r\n- `keyple-java-bom`: `2026.03.19` -> `2026.10.14` (`keyple-card-calypso-java-lib` `3.3.0`, fixing the session signature of the PKI cards when the CA certificate is not registered).\r\n- Android Gradle plugin `8.10.1` -> `9.4.1`, Gradle -> `9.8.1`, Kotlin -> `2.3.21`.\r\n- Multiplatform client: Compose Multiplatform `1.8.2` -> `1.11.1`.\r\n- Sales server: Quarkus `1.8.1.Final` -> `3.40.1` (LTS); dashboard: React `18.2` -> `19.3`, Material UI `5.17` -> `9.4`.\r\n- Sales .NET client: `net7.0` -> `net10.0`.\r\n### Removed\r\n- Coppernic C-One 2 terminal support (plugin not updated since 2022).\r\n- Stored value contract type, which could not be created by the demo.\r\n- Sales Android client: card media other than the contactless card (\"Wearable\" and \"Embedded Secure Element\", which had no reader, and SIM card with the OMAPI reader), with the card media settings.\r\n- Multiplatform client: iOS Intel simulator target, no longer supported by Compose Multiplatform.\r\n- Unused dependencies (dagger-android, RxJava, EventBus, Koin, `log4j`, Material icons extended, etc.), code, and resources."
}
